## The review findings

Finding 1 (the nest specs): `out/storytime-review/batch-13/storytime-nest.png` is a smooth brown
bowl with blue eggs. That is the bowl of eggs of audit E20. The two nest specs no longer use it.
Their color prompts describe the nest in words: a round nest of many thin brown twigs and dry
straw, rough and woven, with the cut ends of the twigs sticking out, in the fork of a branch, with
no bowl and no smooth sides. The picture words are renumbered.

The check of the other 22 specs found one more rejected sheet: the week 2 balls sheet
(`out/storytime/l2/unit1/w02/muse/elements/prop-balls-sheet-m1-color.png`) shows five plain balls
with no pattern, the plain circles of audit E33. The how-many-balls-five spec no longer uses it and
describes the five patterned balls in words. The other rejected sheets (the acorn sheet, the glass
of milk, the alligator, the olive, and the ten plain circles) were already out of the specs of
step 1. The other 21 specs hold no rejected art.

Finding 2 (the judge batch script): a try number is never a file number, because the redraw ids
hold the old approved files m1 to m3 in their week folders. The script now reads the top-level
costs.tsv of the week folder of the spec. A try is a row of that id with kind `color` or `line`
and a time at or after `2026-11-04T07:54:00Z`. The rows in time order are the tries, and try n is
the n-th row. The costs.tsv has a version column, and the script uses it: the color file of a try
is `<id>-m<version>-color.png`. A line row holds the line file name in its output column. A try
that does not exist is an error with a clear message. The `--from` option is gone.

